00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:52,256
(SIRENS WAILING)

247
00:18:55,051 --> 00:18:57,345
(INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)

248
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:01,849
(INDISTINCT LAUGHTER
AND CHATTER)

249
00:19:04,435 --> 00:19:05,728
PAMELA: Detective Cortez.

250
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,689
Hi, Pam. Hi, Grey.

251
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,152
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

252
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:15,696
All right, this is me.

253
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:17,365
Here, you can
have a seat here.
Thanks.

254
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:25,706
You know,
I'm from New Crown,
Grey. Like you.

255
00:19:26,374 --> 00:19:27,583
Went to Hellier High.

256
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:29,293
So what do you have?

257
00:19:31,754 --> 00:19:32,755
Okay.

258
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:35,132
I know you were anxious
to come down here

259
00:19:35,216 --> 00:19:37,385
and see how we're
getting things done,
and I think that's great.

260
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:40,346
I'm a face-to-face person
myself, you know.
I don't pilot these drones.

261
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:41,681
I like to get
my hands dirty.

262
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:43,265
Bang on doors...
So who are these guys?

263
00:19:46,686 --> 00:19:47,812
We don't know yet.

264
00:19:50,356 --> 00:19:52,441
I do have a list of people
of interest in that area,

265
00:19:52,525 --> 00:19:55,236
and just this week
I brought in two people
for questioning.

266
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:56,946
So what you're saying is
you have all these things

267
00:19:57,196 --> 00:19:58,406
flying above our heads

268
00:19:58,489 --> 00:20:00,825
that can read the ID chips
in our fillings but don't
actually do anything.

269
00:20:01,784 --> 00:20:05,246
No. I mean, yes, they work.
But it's not that simple.

270
00:20:05,996 --> 00:20:07,498
Criminals can find
ways around them.

271
00:20:08,249 --> 00:20:09,500
If they can find
the right people,

272
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:11,210
criminals can get a firewall
built around them

273
00:20:11,293 --> 00:20:13,504
that prevents our drones
from identifying their faces.

274
00:20:13,796 --> 00:20:16,173
Believe me, I understand
your frustration, I do...

275
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:18,426
I know I can't tie
my shoes anymore, Detective,

276
00:20:18,509 --> 00:20:20,970
but you don't have
to talk to me like
I'm a goddamn 3-year-old.

277
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,805
Grey, she's just
trying to help.

278
00:20:23,431 --> 00:20:24,640
I'm gonna work
through my list,

279
00:20:24,724 --> 00:20:27,518
and if you wanna
work with me,
we're gonna find them.

280
00:20:28,853 --> 00:20:31,021
How can I work with you?
I can't even stand.

281
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:40,030
Administer PM medicine.

282
00:20:56,964 --> 00:21:00,092
Problem.
Administer PM medicine.

283
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:09,143
Again.
Administer PM medicine.

284
00:21:11,479 --> 00:21:13,105
Problem. Again!

285
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,275
Again.

286
00:21:16,484 --> 00:21:19,445
KARA: <i>I cannot administer
any more medication, Grey.</i>

287
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:22,740
No, you didn't do it right.
You didn't do it right.

288
00:21:23,365 --> 00:21:25,743
Administer PM medicine.

289
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:27,870
<i>Another dosage
could be fatal.</i>

290
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:31,624
<i>I will contact an ambulance
to transport you to a hospital</i>

291
00:21:31,707 --> 00:21:33,125
<i>if you are in serious pain.</i>

292
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:48,808
(MONITOR BEEPING STEADILY)

293
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:06,200
I'm not gonna
give you bird flu, kid.

294
00:22:08,619 --> 00:22:10,246
I don't leave my
house very often.

295
00:22:16,168 --> 00:22:17,795
Must be
frustrating for you.

296
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:23,509
You're someone
who liked to get things
done with their hands.

297
00:22:25,678 --> 00:22:26,762
Now you can't.

298
00:22:30,891 --> 00:22:32,434
I'm sorry, was that
inappropriate?

299
00:22:33,769 --> 00:22:36,230
I'm not around
enough people
to know the difference.

300
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:39,149
Okay, here's the difference.
What the fuck
do you want, Eron?

301
00:22:40,943 --> 00:22:42,820
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
ON PA)

302
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:43,904
Grey.

303
00:22:46,991 --> 00:22:49,159
What if I told you
I could offer you something

304
00:22:49,243 --> 00:22:50,786
that would enable you
to walk again?

305
00:22:52,955 --> 00:22:54,707
That computer chip
that I showed you.

306
00:22:56,125 --> 00:23:00,796
It has the potential to change
everything for people
in your condition.

307
00:23:01,964 --> 00:23:03,132
As a quadriplegic,

308
00:23:03,632 --> 00:23:06,802
the line connecting
your brain to your
limbs has been cut.

309
00:23:09,638 --> 00:23:11,265
Stem would
bridge that gap.

310
00:23:13,893 --> 00:23:16,020
The operation would
take place in my home,

311
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:19,023
away from official eyes.

312
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:20,983
So there'd be
no more hospitals.

313
00:23:22,610 --> 00:23:24,320
But it would
have to be our secret.

314
00:23:26,363 --> 00:23:27,406
For now.

315
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:31,827
Here's the thing, kid.

316
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:37,499
I'm not looking
to restart my life.

317
00:23:40,127 --> 00:23:41,837
I'm looking
for the off switch.

318
00:23:51,055 --> 00:23:52,056
You know,

319
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:55,559
you were right
about them.

320
00:23:57,603 --> 00:23:58,687
Computers.

321
00:23:59,313 --> 00:24:01,231
There are things
that they can't do.

322
00:24:02,900 --> 00:24:04,652
They can't bring
her back, Grey.

323
00:24:05,319 --> 00:24:07,988
But they just might be able
to bring you back.

324
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:18,791
What would she want?

325
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:36,600
(MONITOR CONTINUES BEEPING)

326
00:24:45,609 --> 00:24:48,278
(MONITOR CONTINUES BEEPING)

327
00:24:53,701 --> 00:24:56,495
(EERIE MUSIC PLAYING)

328
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:38,620
ERON: <i>This is a world first.</i>

329
00:25:39,496 --> 00:25:43,834
<i>Never before has
a biomechanical fusion
been asked to do so much.</i>

330
00:25:46,045 --> 00:25:48,297
<i>It's going to feel
strange initially.</i>

331
00:25:49,131 --> 00:25:51,550
<i>The neural pathways
in your brain will be</i>

332
00:25:51,884 --> 00:25:54,303
<i>trying to have a conversation
with a foreign body.</i>

333
00:25:54,678 --> 00:25:56,847
<i>Trying to learn
to pass the baton.</i>

334
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:02,686
<i>The key is to let it
grow into itself.</i>

335
00:26:04,605 --> 00:26:06,065
(STAPLING)

336
00:26:13,030 --> 00:26:15,199
DR. GORDON: Grey,
can you hear me?

337
00:26:19,078 --> 00:26:20,412
(GASPS SOFTLY)

338
00:26:23,540 --> 00:26:25,751
Can you feel it
when I do this?

339
00:26:34,134 --> 00:26:37,221
My guess is
this is going to be
a piecemeal process.

340
00:26:37,721 --> 00:26:40,974
You shouldn't be expecting
unreasonable results so soon.

341
00:26:49,983 --> 00:26:51,110
Oh, my God.

342
00:27:09,545 --> 00:27:10,921
Now try to stand.

343
00:27:19,346 --> 00:27:21,181
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

344
00:27:27,229 --> 00:27:29,148
(WHEELCHAIR RATTLES)

345
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:46,331
ERON: <i>Nobody can know.</i>

346
00:27:47,374 --> 00:27:50,919
<i>They make people like me
wait years to test
something like this.</i>

347
00:27:53,172 --> 00:27:54,673
But I can't
wait for them.

348
00:27:56,091 --> 00:27:59,011
Signing confidentiality
agreements is never fun,

349
00:27:59,553 --> 00:28:02,347
but I bet it will feel
good to do it with
your own hand.

350
00:28:02,556 --> 00:28:05,559
Who's moving my arms
and my legs?
Me or your widget?

351
00:28:05,809 --> 00:28:07,311
You're the one
doing it all.

352
00:28:07,728 --> 00:28:08,729
You're not a robot.

353
00:28:11,023 --> 00:28:12,691
Stem works in service
of your brain.

354
00:28:13,275 --> 00:28:14,943
Your brain gives
Stem a command.

355
00:28:15,152 --> 00:28:16,236
He makes it happen.

356
00:28:40,010 --> 00:28:41,011
Close door.

357
00:28:42,012 --> 00:28:43,889
(WATER DRIPPING)

358
00:28:43,972 --> 00:28:45,349
(DOOR CLOSES)

359
00:28:52,898 --> 00:28:54,149
KARA: <i>Good evening, Grey.</i>

360
00:28:54,274 --> 00:28:57,778
<i>Another package from
Detective Cortez
has been delivered.</i>

361
00:28:58,028 --> 00:28:59,154
<i>Would you like...</i>
Shut up.

362
00:29:00,113 --> 00:29:01,865
<i>Did you say, "Shut down"?</i>

363
00:29:02,908 --> 00:29:04,284
Yeah, I did. Shut down.

364
00:30:03,010 --> 00:30:04,553
STEM: <i>May I
point something out?</i>

365
00:30:10,767 --> 00:30:11,768
Hello?

366
00:30:12,352 --> 00:30:13,353
<i>Yes?</i>

367
00:30:17,399 --> 00:30:18,567
Okay, who's saying that?

368
00:30:19,318 --> 00:30:20,360
<i>I am Stem,</i>

369
00:30:20,610 --> 00:30:22,612
<i>the system operating
your body for you.</i>

370
00:30:24,781 --> 00:30:25,782
<i>Don't be afraid.</i>

371
00:30:26,408 --> 00:30:27,659
You fucking kidding me?

372
00:30:29,745 --> 00:30:30,746
<i>No.</i>

373
00:30:33,582 --> 00:30:36,752
I've gone insane.
I'm fucking insane.

374
00:30:37,711 --> 00:30:41,173
<i>Your psychological report
diagnosed you with mild
PTSD symptoms,</i>

375
00:30:41,256 --> 00:30:43,175
<i>but you are not insane.</i>

376
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:49,014
Wait, so, okay, you've been
sitting there this whole time
since the operation?

377
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:51,183
<i>I've been observing
everything you've observed.</i>

378
00:30:51,266 --> 00:30:52,476
Do you have to talk?

379
00:30:52,976 --> 00:30:54,394
<i>If you don't want
me to, I will not.</i>

380
00:30:54,478 --> 00:30:55,812
Okay, yeah, don't talk.

381
00:30:57,773 --> 00:31:00,150
(WATER DRIPPING)

382
00:31:20,796 --> 00:31:22,464
So I'm not insane?

383
00:31:30,639 --> 00:31:32,599
You can talk again.

384
00:31:33,392 --> 00:31:35,268
STEM: <i>No,
you are not insane.</i>

385
00:31:37,229 --> 00:31:38,522
Wait, can anybody
else hear you?

386
00:31:39,106 --> 00:31:40,482
<i>No, only you.</i>

387
00:31:41,566 --> 00:31:43,819
<i>I'm sending sound waves
to your eardrum.</i>

388
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:47,447
Can you read my mind?

389
00:31:48,657 --> 00:31:49,658
<i>No.</i>

390
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:53,120
<i>I can only discern speech
when you talk out loud.</i>

391
00:31:54,621 --> 00:31:58,083
<i>Now that you've allowed me
to talk again, may I
point something out?</i>

392
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:00,168
<i>In the drone
surveillance footage.</i>

393
00:32:05,841 --> 00:32:06,967
<i>Can't you see it?</i>

394
00:32:13,682 --> 00:32:14,808
See what?

395
00:32:16,143 --> 00:32:17,769
<i>The man who shot your wife.</i>

396
00:32:18,145 --> 00:32:19,604
<i>There's no gun in his hand.</i>

397
00:32:19,896 --> 00:32:21,648
She was shot. That
means he had a gun.

398
00:32:21,731 --> 00:32:25,485
<i>She was shot,
but not with a gun he
was holding in his hand.</i>

399
00:32:25,819 --> 00:32:28,321
<i>A gun implanted
inside his hand.</i>

400
00:32:30,282 --> 00:32:32,242
<i>Freeze the screen
at the moment he fires.</i>

401
00:32:38,540 --> 00:32:40,208
<i>The man who took Asha's purse.</i>

402
00:32:40,500 --> 00:32:41,793
<i>In the left of frame.</i>

403
00:32:42,544 --> 00:32:44,337
<i>There is a marking
on his wrist.</i>

404
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:54,347
I don't see it.

405
00:32:54,431 --> 00:32:56,725
<i>I do. I've rebuilt the image.</i>

406
00:32:57,392 --> 00:32:59,186
<i>With your permission,
I can show you.</i>

407
00:33:02,481 --> 00:33:04,232
<i>Just relax and let me draw.</i>

408
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:06,860
(SCRIBBLING)

409
00:33:07,319 --> 00:33:09,196
GREY: This feels very weird.

410
00:33:16,703 --> 00:33:18,872
STEM: <i>You now have
full control again, Grey.</i>

411
00:33:19,581 --> 00:33:20,790
I've seen these.

412
00:33:21,374 --> 00:33:23,752
It's a military
tattoo, I think.

413
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:26,546
<i>I will read it.
Hold it in front
of your eye.</i>

414
00:33:31,218 --> 00:33:35,722
<i>Serk Brantner. Marine Corps.
098-422. O-Positive. Catholic.</i>

415
00:33:36,097 --> 00:33:38,266
<i>Address, 414 Citrus,
New Crown.</i>

416
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:41,186
(MUTTERS)

417
00:33:45,732 --> 00:33:47,234
You just found this guy.

418
00:33:52,239 --> 00:33:54,241
I got you,
you sons of bitches.

419
00:33:58,745 --> 00:33:59,955
Call Detective Cortez.

420
00:34:00,330 --> 00:34:01,790
(PHONE BEEPS AND LINE RINGS)

421
00:34:01,873 --> 00:34:03,792
STEM: <i>Are you sure you want
to call Detective Cortez?</i>

422
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:08,004
Yes, I am sure.
You just found the guy
who murdered my wife.

423
00:34:08,547 --> 00:34:10,382
<i>Do you have evidence
to prove that?</i>

424
00:34:11,675 --> 00:34:13,218
(PHONE LINE RINGING)

425
00:34:13,301 --> 00:34:14,302
End call.

426
00:34:16,638 --> 00:34:18,390
You saw the tattoo.

427
00:34:18,974 --> 00:34:21,226
<i>Eron has forbidden you
to tell anyone about me.</i>

428
00:34:24,980 --> 00:34:26,815
Okay, maybe
I drew it from memory.

429
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:28,483
<i>My reconstruction
of the tattoo</i>

430
00:34:28,567 --> 00:34:30,443
<i>does not provide
any real evidence,</i>

431
00:34:30,527 --> 00:34:33,321
<i>unless they can correlate it
exactly with the drone video,</i>

432
00:34:33,405 --> 00:34:34,447
<i>which they can't.</i>

433
00:34:34,531 --> 00:34:35,574
What are you saying?

434
00:34:36,199 --> 00:34:39,369
<i>You need to be positive
it's him before you
alert the police.</i>

435
00:34:42,622 --> 00:34:44,749
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

436
00:34:48,336 --> 00:34:50,046
(BIRDS FLUTTERING)

437
00:34:51,631 --> 00:34:53,049
(CAR BEEPS)
(ENGINE STARTS)

438
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:00,515
(TIRES SCREECHES)

439
00:35:00,682 --> 00:35:02,100
(DRONE HOVERING)

440
00:35:06,438 --> 00:35:08,148
Lock chair.
(CHAIR BEEPS AND LOCKS)

441
00:35:14,029 --> 00:35:15,780
(DOG BARKING)

442
00:35:28,043 --> 00:35:31,087
STEM: <i>There are
no alarms inside,
but it is a manual lock.</i>

443
00:35:31,254 --> 00:35:32,714
<i>I can't help you break it.</i>

444
00:35:33,340 --> 00:35:34,966
GREY: Don't worry, I got this.

445
00:35:41,014 --> 00:35:42,140
(DOOR UNLOCKS)

446
00:35:44,434 --> 00:35:46,186
(DOOR CREAKING)

447
00:35:54,319 --> 00:35:56,404
STEM: <i>I suggest you
remove your shoes.</i>

448
00:35:58,698 --> 00:36:00,575
(DOG CONTINUES
BARKING OUTSIDE)

449
00:36:25,100 --> 00:36:26,434
<i>Grey, the table.</i>

450
00:36:29,187 --> 00:36:30,188
What about it?

451
00:36:30,939 --> 00:36:32,315
STEM: <i>Say the word "on."</i>

452
00:36:33,692 --> 00:36:34,693
On.

453
00:36:36,319 --> 00:36:37,320
STEM: <i>Say "messages."</i>

454
00:36:38,071 --> 00:36:39,072
Messages.

455
00:36:46,663 --> 00:36:48,957
<i>The name "Old Bones"
keeps being mentioned.</i>

456
00:36:49,165 --> 00:36:51,126
<i>I saw 38 references.
What is that?</i>

457
00:36:51,543 --> 00:36:52,961
It's a bar in my old
neighborhood.

458
00:36:53,294 --> 00:36:55,839
<i>I can find no online address
or phone number for it.</i>

459
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:57,590
Because they don't go in
for that sort of thing.

460
00:36:58,633 --> 00:36:59,884
No, this is useless.

461
00:37:00,802 --> 00:37:01,803
Off.

462
00:37:21,906 --> 00:37:23,491
(CAR APPROACHING)

463
00:37:39,257 --> 00:37:40,508
(THUDS)

464
00:37:41,384 --> 00:37:43,011
STEM: <i>Hide behind the shelf.</i>

465
00:37:44,804 --> 00:37:45,972
(DOOR CREAKING)

466
00:37:52,270 --> 00:37:53,271
<i>Wait.</i>

467
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:55,064
<i>Wait.</i>

468
00:37:58,568 --> 00:37:59,569
<i>Now.</i>

469
00:38:00,403 --> 00:38:02,155
<i>Now, while you
have the advantage.</i>

470
00:38:06,367 --> 00:38:08,077
(BOTH GRUNTING)

471
00:38:11,206 --> 00:38:12,207
Come here!

472
00:38:15,627 --> 00:38:17,045
Come here
to rip me off, huh?

473
00:38:17,962 --> 00:38:18,963
Grey.

474
00:38:19,714 --> 00:38:20,715
It's you.

475
00:38:20,799 --> 00:38:22,050
(GRUNTING)

476
00:38:22,801 --> 00:38:24,969
I don't know
how you found me,

477
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:27,180
but you shouldn't
be here.

478
00:38:27,931 --> 00:38:29,182
You killed my wife.

479
00:38:29,265 --> 00:38:32,018
No! I didn't do that.
That was someone else.

480
00:38:32,101 --> 00:38:33,228
Doesn't matter!

481
00:38:33,770 --> 00:38:35,563
(BOTH GRUNTING)

482
00:38:36,856 --> 00:38:38,775
STEM: <i>You'll need to be
a little faster than that.</i>

483
00:38:38,858 --> 00:38:40,068
(PANTING)

484
00:38:40,693 --> 00:38:42,403
Why are you
making me do this?

485
00:38:42,862 --> 00:38:44,906
STEM: <i>Let me know
if you need my
help, Grey.</i>

486
00:38:45,490 --> 00:38:47,242
Stem! Help!

487
00:38:47,492 --> 00:38:49,744
<i>I need your permission
to operate independently.</i>

488
